The contract's fair value before any reveal is the expected minimum of the two dealt cards. Counting the 28 possible pairs: min 2 in 7 pairs, min 9 in 11, min 13 in 10. That gives 243/28 ≈ 8.68.

The previous buyer took our ask at 10, which weakly suggests the value is above 10 (more likely if that buyer was informed). I'll nudge the fair value up to roughly 9.5. I'm short one unit, so I'll widen the ask a bit and keep the bid slightly higher to encourage a buy-back.

