Card 1 is 13, so the remaining seven cards are 2, 9, 9, 13, 13, 13, 14. Card 2 is drawn from these, and the settlement is min(13, card 2): 2 with probability 1/7, 9 with 2/7, and 13 with 4/7. The fair value is 72/7 ≈ 10.3.

An informed counterparty sells to me at my bid only when the value is below the bid, and buys from me at my ask only when the value is above it. A bid of 8.9 means only a settlement of 2 can hit it, since 9 is not below 8.9. An ask of 13.0 means a settlement of 13 cannot hit it, since 13 is not above 13. That leaves the informed trader able to hit only the bid, and only in the low-value case, while noise traders still trade on both sides around a fair value near 10.3.

